                            	                    <div class="subtitle">Game On!</div>
                                                    	                   <h2>Feel the Energy and Excitement of Atlantic Cape Buccaneers Athletics</h2>
                                                <p><img alt="women's soccer student athletes in action" class="align-right" height="267" src="../_images/athletics/Women-Soccer-vs-Cumberland-2.jpg" width="400"/>When you don an Atlantic Cape Community College Buccaneers uniform you not only represent the College, but you become a living piece of our athletics program's illustrious and storied history. Today's student-athletes are blazing their own trail of excellence and creating new moments of Buccaneers greatness.</p>
<p>As a Buccaneer you will enjoy the camaraderie and positive team spirit as you compete against other Region 19 schools throughout the state and beyond. Atlantic Cape is part of the&#160;<span>Garden State Athletic Conference (GSAC), which consists of 16 New Jersey-based junior colleges as part of the National Junior College Athletic Association's Region 19.&#160;</span></p>
<p style="text-align: left;"><a class="ctaButton" href="https://fan.hudl.com/usa/nj/mays-landing/organization/134576/atlantic-cape-commun/schedule?date=2024-01-14T05%3A00%3A00.000Z&amp;range=Week&amp;s=U2NoZWR1bGVFbnRyeVB1YmxpY1N1bW1hcnk2NTllYzU1YjY1MmE4NmRlYzI3MGEzMzI%3D"><span>View Live Stream</span></a></p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        
            	    </section>
    	    


    
        
                
       
                            
    	   	<div aria-label="One Column Component 3" class="columns components" role="region">
    		<div class="wrapper">
			<div class="one">
				<div class="cell">
					<div class="content">
						
												 <h2><span style="font-size: 2.25rem;">Atlantic Cape offers 10 athletics programs during Fall and Spring semesters:</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Baseball</strong> plays our national past-time against NJCAA Division III opponents on our new, state-of-the-art Atlantic Cape Baseball Field on our Mays Landing campus behind the Rutgers campus building.</li>
<li><strong>Archery</strong>&#160;competes in&#160;USA Archery's Collegiate Division and boasts an illustrious history with over 50 collegiate All-American Archers and National Champions.</li>
<li><strong>Men's and women's basketball</strong> are exciting, up and coming, perennial contenders in the GSAC and Region 19.</li>
<li><strong>Men's and women's volleyball</strong> play their fast, fun and furious style in our Jonathan Pitney Gymnasium.</li>
<li><strong>Men's and women's soccer</strong> play their games on our refurbished Mays Landing campus soccer field behind the Rutgers campus building and Parking Lot 5.</li>
<li><strong>Women's cross country</strong>&#160;recently completed its second successful season in 2026 and is based out of our Cape May County campus.</li>
<li><strong>Esports&#160;</strong>empowers you to show off your skills and compete with other college-level players in a variety of games.</li>
</ul>
					</div>
									</div>  
			</div>
		</div>
